# Web UX contract

Follow `docs/ux/web-ux-conventions.md` (source of truth). Digest:

- Bottom nav has 5 stable tabs: Home, Orders, Inventory, Customers, More. Do not add/remove tabs without updating that doc.
- Global actions always include Search, New Order, Return, Add Inventory, Scan.
- Thumb-zone primary actions; one dominant choice per step; list/status-first (no chart dashboards in MVP).
- Status colors: Available green, Rented blue, Due Today orange, Overdue red, Archived grey.
- Offline: subtle non-blocking banner only. More-tab offline toggle is demo/simulation, not product positioning.
- Appearance: Dark/Light only; default Dark; More-tab segmented toggle; theme-aware colors via ColorScheme (no light-only hardcodes).
- Forms: items-first New Order (running total; days/amount happy path; Rent/Sell/Job under More options), then phone-first customer attach with optional collapsed Advance; skip customer when issuing from a profile; unit identity optional unless catalog requires it.
- Home defaults: search + KPIs + needsAttention (Quick Actions / Pending jobs via Customize Home; FAB for New Order / Return).
